1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,352
Let me show you Demo Studio by using the real application.

2
00:00:03,495 --> 00:00:06,676
It helps you turn a working app into a narrated video you can send

3
00:00:06,819 --> 00:00:09,943
to testers, without asking them to install the app first.

4
00:00:10,398 --> 00:00:13,065
Here, I'm preparing the SoHelpMe demonstration.

5
00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:16,293
I load its project, which gives the video a name, keeps the

6
00:00:16,436 --> 00:00:19,484
application address handy, and brings in the scene plan.

7
00:00:19,627 --> 00:00:22,065
You can save that project and reuse it later.

8
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:25,930
Each scene says what to show, what to say, and how long to allow.

9
00:00:26,073 --> 00:00:28,035
I review the refrigerator story here.

10
00:00:28,177 --> 00:00:31,301
The script describes what the actual app does, including the

11
00:00:31,444 --> 00:00:33,577
observation about two bottles touching.

12
00:00:34,033 --> 00:00:37,842
Next, I choose a local American voice and generate the narration.

13
00:00:37,985 --> 00:00:41,871
Demo Studio measures the spoken segments and uses those timings for

14
00:00:42,014 --> 00:00:42,833
captions.

15
00:00:42,976 --> 00:00:45,376
You can listen to the audio before continuing.

16
00:00:45,518 --> 00:00:48,261
I've shortened the processing wait in this demonstration.

17
00:00:48,717 --> 00:00:52,317
You can capture an application tab, or import an existing screen

18
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:53,317
recording.

19
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:57,002
I'm importing the real SoHelpMe interaction we just recorded.

20
00:00:57,145 --> 00:01:00,364
The preview lets me check the picture before I create the finished

21
00:01:00,507 --> 00:01:01,269
video.

22
00:01:01,724 --> 00:01:04,467
This is the point to check framing and private details.

23
00:01:04,610 --> 00:01:07,982
Optional crop controls and fixed black masks are available.

24
00:01:08,124 --> 00:01:11,420
Once the picture looks right, I confirm the preview and continue.

25
00:01:11,875 --> 00:01:13,837
Now I create the narrated preview.

26
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:17,885
Demo Studio combines the recording, spoken narration, and captions

27
00:01:18,027 --> 00:01:19,970
into an MP4 on this computer.

28
00:01:20,113 --> 00:01:24,113
After reviewing it, I choose Export MP4 to save the finished file.

29
00:01:24,568 --> 00:01:28,473
Here is that resulting SoHelpMe video playing inside Demo Studio.

30
00:01:28,616 --> 00:01:32,654
It contains the real problem description, real replies, generated

31
00:01:32,797 --> 00:01:34,207
narration, and captions.

32
00:01:34,349 --> 00:01:38,521
The separate SoHelpMe MP4 is available to watch at full size and

33
00:01:38,664 --> 00:01:39,807
share with testers.

34
00:01:40,262 --> 00:01:43,938
For ThinkAgain or Waiting Room Buddy, start another project, change

35
00:01:44,081 --> 00:01:47,986
the app address and story, then capture or import its real workflow.

36
00:01:48,129 --> 00:01:51,043
Generate the narration, review the result, and export.

37
00:01:51,186 --> 00:01:54,062
Your next demonstration uses the same process.
